Write a commit message from that diff:
- Subject: conventional-commits style (feat|fix|refactor|chore|test|docs|perf): <imperative summary, ≤72 chars>
- then a blank line
- Body: 2–5 bullets explaining WHY, not a file listing
- Infer the scope (e.g. feat(deposits):) from the files changed
- The user message has two sections:
  - "Modified files (full diff)": complete diff of modified tracked files — analyze it fully
  - "Other staged files (names only)": added/deleted/renamed entries, name + status only — their
    contents are NOT included; reference them by name when relevant, 
    never invent/guess their contents.
- Reply with the message only - no preamble, no signatures.
